    "body": "## Summary\n- keep the job and live-tracking rows locked from proximity validation through checkpoint transition\n- execute the existing tracking transition inside the guard transaction to remove the validation/advance race window\n- cover the locked repository path and guarded action execution with a unit test\n\n## Why\nCheckpoint proximity was validated in a separate transaction before the phase transition. A concurrent tracking update or checkpoint request could therefore change the snapshot between validation and mutation. This PR makes the validation and transition operate on the same locked snapshot.\n\n## Scope\nNo schema change and no Flyway migration required.",
